    "body": "After updating to pytest 8.3.4 the following code\r\n\r\n```\r\nPython 3.11.10 (main, Nov 20 2024, 15:38:42) [GCC 12.2.0] on linux\r\nType \"help\", \"copyright\", \"credits\" or \"license\" for more information.\r\n>>> import pytest\r\n>>> import numpy as np\r\n>>> np.False_ == pytest.approx(False)\r\n```\r\n\r\nreturns `False` where as it returns `True` with pytest 8.3.3. I would not expect to have to update my code when updating to a patch version.\r\n\r\nI would think, without having any clue, that https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/pull/9354, is the culprit.\r\n\r\n```\r\n$pip list\r\nPackage    Version\r\n---------- -------\r\niniconfig  2.0.0\r\nnumpy      2.2.0\r\npackaging  24.2\r\npip        24.0\r\npluggy     1.5.0\r\npytest     8.3.4\r\nsetuptools 65.5.0\r\n```\r\n\r\nOS: debian bookworm",
